WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
- So you and Nicole just
celebrated your 15th anniversary.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.800
Congratulations.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.633
That's amazing.

00:00:05.633 --> 00:00:07.037
- Thank you.

00:00:07.037 --> 00:00:09.820
- I feel like marriage can
be hard in general, but like,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.400
especially under a microscope,
it can be really hard.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.400
So that's really cool.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.640
And I heard that she
recently said that initially

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.600
you weren't into her.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.150
And I just, here's the question.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.610
Who's not into Nicole Kidman?

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.340
- That's not true, that's not true.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.380
That's why you gotta
have context for things.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.110
- I was like, where was
your bar for humanity?

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.280
If Nicole Kidman didn't make the cut.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.230
- It wasn't how high, it was
how low mine was about myself.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.140
- No!

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:32.973
- Truly.

00:00:32.973 --> 00:00:33.990
This is no, I don't mean that,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.760
literally, I mean, I was like,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.520
there's no way this girl
is interested in me at all.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.870
So someone had given me her number.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.230
I couldn't bring myself
to call that number.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.750
I was so yeah.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.530
- People just came up to you

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.830
and gave you Nicole Kidman's number?

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.130
- No, no, that's a whole different story.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.063
- Okay, I was like, I want your life.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.520
- Point of this story was it was more just

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.353
- [Kelly] You were nervous about it.

00:00:56.353 --> 00:00:57.186
- I was nervous, yeah.

00:00:57.186 --> 00:00:58.019
- Oh, okay.

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:00.350
So what, you also speaking
where you did a song

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.850
for "9 Perfect Strangers," right?

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.045
I love the show that she did.

00:01:03.045 --> 00:01:03.878
- "Crimson Blue"

00:01:03.878 --> 00:01:05.260
- Yeah, did she ask you to do that?

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.000
Or were you like into doing that?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
- We wanted to write some
songs and Nick said, you know,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:10.910
could you write some songs

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.840
maybe that would work in
"9 Perfect Strangers"?

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.140
And so a couple of friends of mine and I

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.610
wrote a whole bunch of songs
and they chose "Crimson Blue."

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.510
- That's so cool.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.980
- Yeah, it was wild because
the director said, can you

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.540
I said, what's the directive of this?

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.373
What do you want?

00:01:23.373 --> 00:01:24.206
What sort of song you want?

00:01:24.206 --> 00:01:28.210
And he said kind of
trippy, Pink Floyd-ish,

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.020
with sort of Eastern
meditative, ethereal, go ahead.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.412
I'm like, what?

00:01:34.412 --> 00:01:38.170
I wrote I never saw the sky Crimson Blue

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.560
kaleidoscope my eyes, shapes and hues.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.320
So we may as well been high writing that.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.153
- I'm so into that.

00:01:43.153 --> 00:01:44.980
I feel like I'm reading
"Alice in Wonderland."

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.480
I heard that she was in
character the whole time.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.560
Like she said she was in character.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.451
Was she in character
the whole time at home?

00:01:52.451 --> 00:01:53.430
- No, not at home.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.010
- 'Cause I'm like if you were coming home

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.060
to that every night,

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.090
it's amazing that you made it 15 years.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:58.923
That's creepy.

00:01:58.923 --> 00:02:00.161
- It's pretty sexy.

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:01.640
- Kinda creepy as well.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:02.473
She kinda, I was like,

00:02:02.473 --> 00:02:05.860
I can't tell if she's really
stage five creepy or like cool.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.620
Or like she had me
guessing the whole time.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:08.890
- You have creepy in stages.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:09.723
I like this.

00:02:09.723 --> 00:02:10.756
- [Kelly] I actually like creepy.

00:02:10.756 --> 00:02:12.040
- Stage five creepy.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:12.970
- [Kelly] I'm really into creepy.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.260
- How many stages are there by the way?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.143
- 11, Spinal Tap. (laughs)

